{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/variantprotocol\/refsink()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantProtocol"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantProtocol\/refSink()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" uses a floating reference count system.  All functions with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names starting with "},{"code":"g_variant_new_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" return floating","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"references.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refSink"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"VariantRef","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib10VariantRefV"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}],"role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GLib","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"externalID":"s:4GLib15VariantProtocolPAAE7refSinkAA0B3RefVSgyF","title":"refSink()"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refSink"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantRef","text":"VariantRef","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib10VariantRefV"},{"text":"!","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_variant_ref_sink()"},{"type":"text","text":" on a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" with a floating reference","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"will convert the floating reference into a full reference.  Calling","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_variant_ref_sink()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on a non-floating "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant"},{"type":"text","text":" results in an"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"additional normal reference being added."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In other words, if the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value"},{"type":"text","text":" is floating, then this call “assumes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"ownership” of the floating reference, converting it to a normal","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"reference.  If the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value"},{"text":" is not floating, then this call adds a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"new normal reference increasing the reference count by one."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All calls that result in a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instance being inserted into a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"container will call ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_variant_ref_sink()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the instance.  This means","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that if the value was just created (and has only its floating","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"reference) then the container will assume sole ownership of the value","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at that point and the caller will not need to unreference it.  This"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"makes certain common styles of programming much easier while still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"maintaining normal refcounting semantics in situations where values"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"are not floating."}]}]}],"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/VariantProtocol/refSink()":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/variantprotocol\/refsink()","title":"refSink()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" uses a floating reference count system.  All functions with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"names starting with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_variant_new_"},{"text":" return floating","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"references."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"refSink","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"text":"VariantRef","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib10VariantRefV"},{"text":"!","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantProtocol\/refSink()"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/VariantProtocol":{"role":"symbol","title":"VariantProtocol","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/variantprotocol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"VariantProtocol","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"VariantProtocol","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"code":"GVariant","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a variant datatype; it can contain one or more values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"along with information about the type of the values."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantProtocol","type":"topic"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/VariantRef":{"url":"\/documentation\/g